Falsifies `file_allocation_table::format::verification::a_geometry_parses_back_to_itself`.

The defect: the table is checked against the clusters alone and not the two reserved entries as well, which is the fault Microsoft's own sizing has when a volume divides it exactly, so the format writes a table one entry short.

Expected to fail: the harness's `.expect("the reader accepts what the format wrote")`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/format.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/format.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/format.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/format.rs
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@ impl Geometry {
                 .ok_or(GeometryError::TooSmall)?;
             clusters = data_sectors / cluster_sectors;
             let capacity = u64::from(table_sectors) * u64::from(bytes) * 8 / bits;
-            if capacity < u64::from(clusters) + 2 {
+            if capacity < u64::from(clusters) {
                 table_sectors += 1;
                 continue;
             }
